WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.645
The CIS Controls include Implementation Groups, often called IG1, IG2, and IG3.

2
00:00:06.645 --> 00:00:13.410
These groups help organizations prioritize activities based on risk, complexity, and available resources.

3
00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:21.382
Smaller organizations often begin with IG1, while larger or more complex environments may implement additional safeguards.

4
00:00:21.382 --> 00:00:26.431
Implementation Groups recognize that organizations have different needs and maturity levels.

5
00:00:26.431 --> 00:00:33.116
A small team with limited resources may need a different starting point than a large enterprise with complex systems.

6
00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:35.890
This structure helps make the controls practical.

7
00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:41.388
It gives organizations a way to sequence improvement without losing sight of long-term maturity.
